<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p class="updated">
Last updated: July 2026
</p>

<p>
Longboard Speedometer is designed with privacy in mind. We do not require an account,
do not sell your information, and do not collect personal data for advertising or analytics.
</p>

<h2>Location Data</h2>

<p>
Longboard Speedometer requests access to your device's location in order to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Measure your speed</li>
    <li>Record your ride route</li>
    <li>Calculate distance traveled</li>
    <li>Calculate elevation changes</li>
</ul>

<p>
Location data is used only while recording rides and is stored locally on your device.
We do not receive or store your location on our servers.
</p>

<h2>Ride Data</h2>

<p>
Ride information, including speed, route, elevation, weather, and ride statistics,
is stored locally on your device.
</p>

<p>
We do not upload your rides to our servers.
</p>

<h2>Accounts</h2>

<p>
Longboard Speedometer does not require you to create an account.
</p>

<h2>Analytics</h2>

<p>
Longboard Speedometer does not use third-party analytics or advertising services.
</p>

<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>
The app may use Apple services, such as Apple Maps or Apple's weather services,
to provide functionality. Those services are governed by Apple's own privacy policies.
</p>

<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

<p>
Longboard Speedometer is not directed toward children under the age of 13 and does
not knowingly collect personal information from children.
</p>

<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

<p>
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p>
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at
<a href="mailto:longboardspeedometer@gmail.com">
longboardspeedometer@gmail.com
</a>.
</p>

<p>
Need help using the app? Visit our
<a href="support.html">Support Page</a>.
</p>

